WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.400
-Hey, everyone, it is Nana Week.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.634
And my new children's book,

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.000
"Nana Loves You More,"
is out today!

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.767
It's pub day.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:07.934
♪♪

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.434
It is -- They call --
They call it "pub day."

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:15.801
-"Pub day."
-Publishing day.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:17.267
-Oh.
-And it's called pub day.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.901
It's a little
inside business -- Yeah.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.067
-So you go to a pub.

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:21.834
-I went to a pub and got
smashed, today, yeah.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:22.834
-Yeah.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.467
-No, I got a lot of
"Happy pub day,"

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:25.467
and that's what it means.

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:27.267
-Oh.
-Publishing. Yeah.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.334
Do you want me
to read you a page?

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.033
-Please.
-Which one?

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.968
-Not the super-sad one.
I don't want to cry.

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.334
-No, there's only one kind of
little sad one in there.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.901
But it's not that sad.
-Read that one.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.834
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.567
Whew!

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:42.901
You picked a good one.
-Oh!

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:46.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:48.901
♪♪

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:53.300
-"More than gold
or treasure or money?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.701
"You are my treasure.
You are my honey."

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.634
[ Audience "Awws" ]
-Oh!

00:00:57.634 --> 00:00:59.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:04.667
Oh!

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.667
-Whew!
-Snap!

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:11.267
-Anyway, that's just one of
the memories you'll make

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:12.901
when you read this.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.033
-And it's $16,000?
-$16,000, yes.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.601
-Wow!
-In crypto bucks.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.133
-Oh, crypto bucks.
-Yeah.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:23.767
You play 30 Jimmy Coin for this,
and you get --

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:25.534
It's only worth --
It's like 4 Ethereum.

00:01:25.534 --> 00:01:27.701
You get --
You get 30 Jimmy Coin.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.634
-Right. Some Ape Coin.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:30.934
-Yep, you get Ape Coin,
of course.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.901
Obviously, Doge Dollar.
You get --

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.634
-Kohl's Cash.
-Yep.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:37.267
You get, uh -- Yeah.
Desk Coin. You can get that.

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.467
You trade in that.
You got to wait a week.

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:40.834
-You got to wait a week
or else it transforms.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.267
-Oh, it's going to go down.
You lose all your money.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.334
If you buy this now,
it'll go down.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:45.701
I would wait a week,
then buy this.

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:46.701
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:47.734
-And then...
[ Whistles ]

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.534
-Yeah, then --
-Then sell it again.

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.133
-Yeah, as an NFT.

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.200
-As an NFT.
-Right.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.467
-Then buy it back
with the American dollar.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.000
-Yeah.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.000
-Sell it for gas money.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.868
-So, all week long,
we're giving some love

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.734
to all the grandmas out there,
all the nanas,

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:05.100
all the gam-gams, all meemaws.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.334
Yeah, all the nonnas.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:07.734
-Abuelas!

00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:10.267
-The abuelas in the world.
Without you, what would we be?

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.767
We love you.

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:13.300
And to show you
how much we love you,

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.267
each night this week,
we're shining a spotlight on

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.501
a talented grandma on our show.

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:20.067
So, tonight's nana is
Dorothea Taylor.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:21.634
She is 71 years old

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:23.767
and she's from
Myrtle Beach, South Carolina.

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:25.901
And tonight, she's going to
play the drums for us.

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.033
Come on out here, Dorothea.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:34.501
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:40.534
Dorothea,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:41.634
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.467
I know you have three children.

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:44.834
How many grandkids do you have?

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.167
-I have two grandchildren --

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:49.801
one 13, who's going to be
a musician, too,

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:51.400
and an 8-month-old.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.434
-Oh, come on.

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:53.434
Well, you're gonna love
that book.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.334
-Brand-new.
-Congratulations.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:56.868
You're going to play
the drums for us,

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:59.400
but I heard that you had
a special request.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.367
-I would love to have
a drum-off with Questlove.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:05.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:10.434
-A drum-off with Questlove.
Now we're talking!

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.434
Are these drums
perfectly fine for you here?

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:13.767
-These are perfectly fine.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:16.300
I have a kit just like this at
home that I gig out with.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.434
-Yeah. Perfect.

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:19.300
Then why don't you get up there,
get ready to go.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.567
We're gonna start this drum-off.
Can I do anything for you?

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.234
♪♪

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:27.601
How long have you been
playing the drums?

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:29.501
-58 years.
-Hey!

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:32.200
That's what I'm talking about.
I think you know what's up.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.634
Quest, you better bring -- You
better bring your A-game, buddy.

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:35.801
-I hope so.

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.767
I've only been playing for
58 months.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:39.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:42.100
-Dorothea, whenever you're
ready, let the drum-off begin.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.601
-Okay.
♪♪

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:05.100
♪♪

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:16.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:45.534
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:47.501
Yes! [ Laughs ]

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.300
Yeah!

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.767
Yeah!
[ Laughs ]

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.234
Come -- Just...

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:58.000
Just don't even.

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:02.033
Yeah, that's right, yeah.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:04.234
Dorothea, wait.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.067
I have an idea
for this last one.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:07.467
That was amazing, by the way.

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:10.000
For this last one, how about
something that Questlove himself

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.100
had a little trouble
doing when --

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.133
-Phil?

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:14.467
-Phil Collins --
-Ah, man, come on!

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:16.501
-Phil Collins was on the show,

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:19.868
and we really hyped up that solo
from "In the Air Tonight,"

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:22.534
the...
[ Imitating drum fill ]

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:27.033
And then when Phil came on to
play it with us and Quest,

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.868
I just kind of snuck around
and stared at Quest for like --

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:32.868
-You startled me
right at that moment.

00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:33.934
-Can you -- What do you think?

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.334
Can you do the
classic drum solo from

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:36.601
"In the Air Tonight,"
Phil Collins?

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:38.133
-I'll try it.
-Okay, buddy.

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:40.467
-Okay.
-Alright, Dorothea.

00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:45.834
That's it! That's how you do it!
♪♪

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:48.567
That's right!

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.400
Give it up for
Dorothea Taylor, everybody!

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:54.067
Stick around.

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:56.334
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:05:56.334 --> 00:05:57.901
Come on back.
♪♪

